percentage of the control growth rate in&#xD;
medium containing 30 ,tg/ml of Met and&#xD;
are derived from the linear portions of the&#xD;
growth curves. Although there is some&#xD;
reduction in growth of the normal cell line&#xD;
at low homocysteine concentrations,&#xD;
optimal growth is observed in medium&#xD;
containing only 0-66mM homocysteine. In&#xD;
contrast none of the tumour lines show&#xD;
optimal growth in medium containing&#xD;
